tt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.5.dev5.official [64b09905c], v4.5.beta1.official [46c495ca2]\n- Not reproducible in: v4.5.dev4.official [209a446e3] and earlier versions\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta1 - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 10 Jun 2025 15:10:17 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 575.57.08) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-9700K CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 31.12 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running a project in a web browser controller input stops working after its first event(s). For example when pressing and releasing D-pad down button only the first event is received. Release event is not received. Refreshing the page or re-running the project is needed in order to receive some controller input again.\n\nAdditional testing:\nPressing LT or RT doesn't cause any events to be received but also blocks subsequent controller events.\nMoving left stick initially causes 2 events to be received one for axis 0 and one for axis 1 respectively.\nMoving right stick initially causes 4 events to be received repeatedly over and over. Two events for axis 4 and two for axis 5 respectively. Half of those events have zero value.\n\nEDIT: Did some more testing under Windows 10 and Firefox and it is also reproducible there. There I received 4-5 events when pressing sticks or triggers (no infinite repeats) and 1 event using buttons.\n\nTested with Microsoft Xbox Series S|X Controller with both wired and wireless connection. Connection type doesn't seem to make a difference here.\nTested under Linux using Firefox 139.0.4 (64-bit) and also under Chromium 137.0.7151.119 with similar results.\n\nKeywords: joypad, gamepad\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the MRP in a web browser and try using a controller. Press D-pad down button a few times and notice that only the first button press was registered.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[controller-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20809953/controller-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107697/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}